WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:11.990
Well, especially when there was bad weather
or foul weather ... we didn't have an indoor

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.539
court to go to.

00:00:14.539 --> 00:00:26.590
So we would take our basketball and go up
to the gym.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.699
Is that the Armory?

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:36.930
Yeah, we used to go in there and they'd chase
us around, the police.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:45.129
And then we found the Walker Auditorium, Walker
Gym where not many people went to.

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:48.690
So we'd go up there and play basketball.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:56.670
My first connection with MIT was probably
when I was about six or seven years old, when

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:00.280
we were wandering and they'd put down granite
floors in the building.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.510
And we'd be, like, belly-surfing on the floors.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:10.390
Sliding on the floors that go into the revolving
door.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.110
Or just running around there know that we're
not supposed to be out of our neighborhood.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:19.510
We'd be up in Walker Memorial in the gym when
it was cold and we couldn't go to other facilities,

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.230
and we'd be playing basketball.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:26.150
And we weren't a group of kids that got in
trouble at MIT.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:30.030
We were a group of kids that when the MIT
police officers would come and say "Guys,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.860
I've got to shut it down.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.180
You have to leave, you know you're not supposed
to be here," we would leave.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.890
But we would roam.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:43.750
Now we're moving on to what is called Chocolate
City, which is a minority dormitory.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.960
You have The Ghetto, the radio station.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:54.811
So now you're talking about the 70s, and going
into '74, '75 where out of high school we're

00:01:54.811 --> 00:02:01.810
still going to the parties, we're listening
to The Ghetto, we're going over to the Coop,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.450
sitting up there in the cafeteria up there
now.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.000
And we fit in.

